id: pm-rust-2di7
title: Live differential conformance suite against the published Node pm CLI
description: "A test that runs the real published Node pm binary and the Rust binary over twin fixture workspaces with the same inputs and asserts resulting .toon and .jsonl bytes match, using the SDK workspace recipe clock for determinism."
type: Task
status: closed
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-08-22T10:41:27.180Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-27T21:33:02.413Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-27T00:44:31.660Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-27T00:44:31.660Z"
author: pi-agent
acceptance_criteria: "The test executes both binaries; it does not read recorded fixtures only;the test is skipped with a clear message when no Node pm installation is available;create, update, comment, and close outputs are compared byte for byte"
parent: pm-rust-u4al
comments[4]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-22T11:36:10.339Z",pi-agent,"Added tests/conformance_differential.rs. The suite locates the real published Node pm installation (PM_NODE_CLI or PATH probe), initializes one fixture workspace with it, clones the tracker for the Rust side, then runs the same five-operation sequence (create, update, comment, status update, close) against both binaries and asserts .toon and .jsonl bytes are identical after every step. The published side runs under its own workspace-recipe facility (fixed clock, zero tick) with wall-clock Date pinned, so all timestamps are deterministic. Verified live against global @unbrained/pm-cli 2026.8.21: identical bytes at every step. A deliberate sabotage (one changed word) made the test fail, proving it compares real output rather than skipping. Skips with an explicit notice when no Node CLI is present."
  "2026-08-27T10:19:34.762Z",claude,"Recording the changed file in structured metadata rather than only in prose: tests/conformance_differential.rs is the differential driver this task's evidence depends on, and it was named in the close reason but absent from the files list, so a reader querying the tracker would not have found it."
  "2026-08-27T10:24:05.644Z",claude,"Ordering note on this record's own evidence, raised in review: the conformance-test evidence was appended before the task was claimed, so the audit trail shows execution preceding ownership. The evidence itself is accurate and the tests it cites pass; what is wrong is the order in which the tracker learned about them. Recorded here as a follow-up rather than rewritten, because the history is append-only, and noted as a process correction: claim first, then execute, then record."
  "2026-08-27T20:19:30.061Z",pi-agent,"Follow-up audit entry recorded under established ownership (item claimed by pi-agent) to correct the order in which this tracker learned the conformance-test evidence. Restated evidence: tests/conformance_differential.rs runs the real published Node pm binary and the Rust binary over the same five-operation sequence (create, update, comment, status update, close) across twin fixture workspaces and asserts .toon and .jsonl bytes are identical at every step; verified live against global @unbrained/pm-cli 2026.8.21 with identical bytes at every step, a deliberate one-word sabotage made the test fail (proving a real comparison rather than a skip), and it skips with an explicit notice when no Node CLI is present. This evidence was originally appended in history events that precede the claim (the comment_add at 2026-08-22T11:36:10Z, the tests_add at 2026-08-27T00:43:51Z, and the docs_add at 2026-08-27T00:43:52Z, all before the claim at 2026-08-27T00:44:26Z). It is restated here under established ownership rather than by rewriting the append-only, hash-chained history."
